WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.356
Do societies need inequality to

2
00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:05.379
work? Two functionalists said yes.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.480
In 1945,

4
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.548
Davis and Moore argued that

5
00:00:08.548 --> 00:00:11.024
unequal rewards attract talent to

6
00:00:11.024 --> 00:00:12.449
important jobs.

7
00:00:12.449 --> 00:00:13.569
In 1953,

8
00:00:13.569 --> 00:00:16.294
Melvin Tumin replied.

9
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.245
Who decides which jobs are

10
00:00:18.245 --> 00:00:20.984
important? And inequality itself stops

11
00:00:20.984 --> 00:00:23.842
talented poor children from rising.

12
00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:25.799
Mobility can be vertical or

13
00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:28.445
